WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.819 --> 00:00:09.751
By now we know how Sexual reproduction in
plants takes place. This is what

00:00:09.751 --> 00:00:14.340
we have learned. The flower which is the reproductive
organ of the plant,

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:17.340
bears the male and the female parts.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:21.619
The male part - the stamen contains the male
gamete while the female part -

00:00:21.619 --> 00:00:28.730
the pistil has the female gamete. Fusion of
the two gives rise to an embryo.

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:33.890
Now let us get to know how exactly the process
occurs. Let us learn about it in

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:38.300
detai!
But before that, tell me one thing - do all

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:44.219
flowers always possess both the floral
parts together? Some of them do.

00:00:44.219 --> 00:00:48.190
What do we call the types of flowers which
possess both the male and female

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:53.270
floral parts together? Flowers which contain
both stamen and pistil together

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:59.699
are called Bisexual flowers. Can you name
a few examples of such types? Rose,

00:00:59.699 --> 00:01:05.751
China rose are a few in this category.
what about other flowers then? Don’t they

00:01:05.751 --> 00:01:11.210
contain both the male and female
floral parts together? some flowers such as

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:16.070
those of Gourd and Pumpkin
possess either stamen, or pistil. That is

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:20.490
the reason why such flowers are called
Unisexual Flowers.

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:25.320
Now getting back to the process, the first
step is that of Pollination. It is

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:29.520
the&nbsp;process&nbsp;by which pollen grains are transferred
to the female reproductive

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:34.009
organs of a plant.
In other words, pollen from the Anther are

00:01:34.009 --> 00:01:39.060
transferred to the stigma
does this process occur only between two flowers

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:44.000
of the same type? Yes, that
is correct. Pollination occurs between the

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:48.840
flowers belonging to the same type.
And does that mean pollination occurs only

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:52.200
between two flowers borne on the
same plant?

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:57.450
that question leads us to the types of Pollination.
The type in which pollination occurs between

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:02.590
flowers borne on the same plant
is called as Self Pollination. So what will

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:07.909
the next type be? The other type of
pollination is called Cross Pollination where

00:02:07.909 --> 00:02:12.670
the pollens travel from the anther
to the stigma of a different flower on another

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:16.109
plant.
can you guess how this process of transfer

00:02:16.109 --> 00:02:22.750
of pollen grains occurs? For this,
there are several agents which aid the process.

00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:27.850
Agents such as wind and water
are the abiotic ones. On the other hand, biotic

00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:34.269
pollinators such as bees, bats,
moths and birds also help in the process.

00:02:34.269 --> 00:02:38.419
The process of pollination makes sure that
the pollen grain safely lands on the

00:02:38.419 --> 00:02:44.949
stigma. But what happens next? Does this lead
to fertilisation directly? Or are

00:02:44.949 --> 00:02:49.940
there any intermediate steps? We will answer
all these questions in the next

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:50.420
video!

